{{Quote|It's like I always say, moisture farming is about communication. And condensation.|A [[Unidentified Weequay technician|Weequay moisture farmer]] to [[Kay Vess]]|audio=MoistureFarmingIsAboutCommunicationAndCondensation-Outlaws.flac|<ref name="Outlaws">''[[Star Wars Outlaws]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Nebit.png|thumb|right|300px|Owen Lars and his nephew, [[Luke Skywalker]], were moisture farmers.]]
A '''moisture farmer''' or '''vapor farmer''' was an individual who operated a [[moisture farm]],<ref name="Episode 4">{{Film|IV}}</ref>> using [[Moisture vaporator|vaporators]] to harvest excess humidity in the [[atmosphere]].<ref name="CL">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> On [[Star|sun]]-scorched [[Planet|worlds]] like [[Tatooine]], many settlers in the [[desert]] were moisture [[farmer]]s.<ref name="Star Wars 7">[[Star Wars (2015) 7|''Star Wars'' (2015) 7]]</ref> Notable examples included members of the [[Lars family]], such as [[Cliegg Lars|Cliegg]], his son [[Owen Lars|Owen]], and the latter's [[Marriage|wife]] [[Beru Whitesun Lars|Beru]].<ref name="Episode II">{{Film|II}}</ref>

Moisture farmers built their homesteads to be partially buried in the ground, as this protected them from wind and heat and kept the residence cool.<ref name="VE">''[[Star Wars: The Visual Encyclopedia]]''</ref> Many farmers would use [[flyhorn lizard]]s to indicate their humidity yield.<ref name="Gameplay Easter Eggs">{{UbisoftYouTube|490LVhVGAqo|Star Wars Outlaws Official Gameplay: All the Star Wars Lore, Details & Easter Eggs &#124; Ubisoft Forward}}</ref>

